  * old ≠ new: n_e = 100: ω2 = 20; n_e = 100: VM = 0.2; n_e = 100: K = 2000
  conv: the old iteration converged; dead1: "no population" at the variance of N = K (first step); dead+: the iteration jumped to
  "no population" at a later step; cyc: no convergence in 100 steps. R·W̄(V(K)) ≤ 1 means a population of size K with its house-of-Gauss variance
  cannot replace itself at lag 0. f(V) is the variance that the population sized by V holds; it falls with V, so V = f(V) has one root.
  new against all states: largest relative difference 3.21e-14

